  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ghormeh sabzi ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ghormeh-sabzi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", the stew every Iranian cook knows by heart. The key step is frying the herbs until very dark before adding any liquid. That process drives off moisture and concentrates the grassy, slightly bitter flavour that defines the dish. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "khoresh ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "khoresh"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", it is always served over plain white rice. The long cook time is not optional . at least two hours of simmering is what turns the stew from pleasant to extraordinary."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
